W:1. When Boney commanded his army to stand,
W:He leveled his cannon right over the land.
W:And he leveled his cannon, the victory to gain,
W:And he slew my light horseman returning from Spain.
W:
W:[Chorus:]
W:Broken-hearted I'll wander, broken-hearted I'll remain,
W:Since my bonnie light horseman in the war he was slain.
W:
W:2. Oh if I were a small bird and had wings to fly,
W:I would fly cross the salt sea to where he does lie,
W:And with my fond wings I'd beat over his grave,
W:And kiss the cold lips that lie cold in the clay.
W:
W:[Chorus]
